course: dictionary
lesson: 3268
title: Words for time: era
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An era is a long period of time, often known for special things that happened in it. Look at the words around it: «In the Han era Chinese thinkers used magnetic spoons for divination.» The sentence tells you what people did in that time, so an era must be a period of history.
explain: Era can also mean a very long time in Earth's history. «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic.» The word "divided" is your clue: Earth's history is cut into named parts, and an era is one of those parts.
explain: An era can also be a time that begins with something new. «The end of an era» means something important has finished, and «the era of smartphones» means a time when smartphones were everywhere. Try "time" in the sentence instead of era. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: An era is a long period of time with special features or events.
fact: In history, we talk about eras such as the Victorian era or the Tudor era.
fact: In science, an era is a very long period of Earth's history, like the Mesozoic Era when dinosaurs lived.
fact: «A new era» means a time when something different begins, and «the end of an era» means something important has finished.
exercise: «In the Han era Chinese thinkers used magnetic spoons for divination.» What does era mean here? | A kind of compass for the sea | *A long period of time in history | A short walk to the village | A large wooden spoon
exercise: Ella says «the end of an era» means the end of a race. What does it really suggest? | The weather is changing | *Something important has finished | A race has just begun | A new spoon has been made
exercise: Jayden says era is a type of dinosaur. What is an era? | A kind of rock found on beaches | A type of dinosaur with long teeth | A very small animal that lives in water | *A long period of time in Earth's history
test: «Foot binding spread from the Song era.» What is the best meaning of era in this sentence? | A village by the river | A kind of small shoe | *A long period of time | A single day in spring
test: Nadia says the Mesozoic Era is a cave where dinosaurs lived. What is it really? | A cave in the mountains | *A very long period of Earth's history | A museum about dinosaurs | A type of rock found by the sea
exam: Which phrase means a time when something new has started? | *A new era | A broken spoon | Sad news | A long walk home
